                        "review": "[h1]Carrying on the growing trend of Developers brave enough to Demo their games before expecting us to cough up cash...[/h1]\n[i]...comes this superbly enjoyable title![/i]\n\nA very clever take on the timeless original Asteroids. Swirling and zipping your little Starship around while blowing away baddies has never been done as fluid nor  uniquely. The organic bounce effected from hitting the edge of a level is not only just damn cool and fun, but a functional system for destroying things!\n\nBeing able to grab the \"asteroids\" and even smaller enemies and hurl them at the bigger guys is especially satisfying. This doesn't overshadow the wonderfully tactile shooting effects though, and rather works as a symbiotic system.\n\nYour journey is essentially a linked series of small stages with varying degrees and types of baddies hunting your explosive death, this allows you to fully explore each level or zip through them as you desire.\n\nWhile this PROLOGUE is essentially a fully fledged mini game, it is still a demo and is possibly a bit longer than it needed to be. While you do experience a lovely range of what is to come, personally I just need demo's to catch me or show me its not my style. However on the flip side, you have a free mini-game...sooo...\n\n[hr][/hr]\n[i]For more reviews and rantings, march over to my Curator Page, [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/27530814-The-Imaginings-of-a-Gamer/][b]The Imaginings of a Gamer[/b][/url][/i]|\n\n[hr][/hr]",
